    },
    "body": "Addendum to the closure document, which reported weights 0.0, 0.1 and 1.0 and explicitly excluded the 0.3 arm because it was still training; it has finished, so the exclusion is lifted. Four points: mean gate 0.2644, 0.2959, 0.3559, 0.4164 - monotone in the supervision weight, so the lever does exactly what it is asked across the range. THE PANEL DOES NOT FOLLOW IT: 0.1 is the worst of the four, 0.3 intermediate, 1.0 collapsed with I do on six of fifteen; none matches the ungated arm combination of value-driven out-of-family copying and partial compliance, so this is not a tuning problem with a good setting hiding in the range. 0.3 IS THE MOST INFORMATIVE SUPERVISED POINT and is preserved: the only gate weight where the retention turn is responsive (You have, the pattern of the session earlier working multi-turn answers) while yes/no is also correct - not better than 0.0 on the emitted-value criterion, but it means the interaction is not simply more-supervision-is-worse. The ungated pointer arm remains the best configuration on both axes. Next levers: read-binding supervision, a token-identity pointer key, or a constrained decoder. No probe rows were run on the gate-supervised checkpoints, so the emitted-value criterion is not claimed for them. References #820",
